course: dictionary
lesson: 5304
title: Karaoke and words from Japan
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some English words come from other languages. Context helps you understand them. «From Japanese came "tsunami", "emoji" and "karaoke" (empty orchestra).» The bracket gives the clue: karaoke means empty orchestra, which is a band playing without its singer.
explain: Karaoke means singing along to recorded music while the words of the song show on a screen, for fun. Try the swap test: «We are having a karaoke night on Friday» fits if you think of a fun party with singing. The meaning makes sense in the sentence.
explain: A karaoke machine is the equipment that plays the music and shows the words. A karaoke night is the party or event. In music lessons, karaoke helps you practise singing.
fact: Karaoke means singing along to recorded music while the words appear on a screen, for fun.
fact: A karaoke machine is the equipment, and a karaoke night is the event.
fact: Karaoke comes from Japan, and it came into English from Japanese.
fact: The sentence says the literal meaning is "empty orchestra".
fact: Phrases to know: «sing karaoke», «karaoke night», «karaoke machine».
exercise: Which language did karaoke come from? | Italian | *Japanese | Scots | Australian English
exercise: Mia says, «We are having a karaoke night on Friday.» What is a karaoke night? | A quiz about maths | *A fun evening of singing along to recorded music with the words on a screen | A night when the children sleep at school | A concert where nobody sings
exercise: Find and copy the word that means singing along to music with the words on a screen. | *karaoke | orchestra | tsunami | emoji
test: Karaoke means singing along to recorded music with the words on a screen, for fun. Which phrase names the equipment that plays the music? | karaoke night | sing karaoke | karaoke party | *karaoke machine
test: Why might a music teacher use karaoke in lessons? | To teach Japanese only | *To help the class practise singing with the words in front of them | To learn to play the drums | To make the class silent
exam: Using the bracket clue in «From Japanese came "tsunami", "emoji" and "karaoke" (empty orchestra)», what does karaoke literally mean? | A party with no music | A picture with a character | A wave in the harbour | *An empty orchestra
